"""Upgrade selected recall questions to statement-based UPSC-style discriminators."""
import json,pathlib,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def amend(month,num,question,correct,wrongs,explanation):
 p=R/'data'/f'{month}-mcqs.json';Q=json.loads(p.read_text());q=Q[num-1];opts=[correct]+wrongs.split('|');random.Random(month+str(num)+'review').shuffle(opts);q.update(question=question,options=opts,answer=opts.index(correct),explanation=explanation);p.write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
choices='1 only|2 only|Neither 1 nor 2'
amend('june',1,'Consider the June 2025 MPC decision: (1) Repo was cut by 50 basis points to 5.5%. (2) The stance changed to neutral. Which are correct?','Both 1 and 2',choices,'Both are correct. A neutral stance preserves flexibility and does not prohibit a simultaneous rate cut; 50 basis points is 0.5 percentage point.')
amend('june',2,'Consider balance-of-payments statements: (1) A current-account surplus requires a goods-trade surplus. (2) A Q4 surplus necessarily establishes a full-year surplus. Which are correct?','Neither 1 nor 2','1 only|2 only|Both 1 and 2','Services, income and transfers also enter the current account. Other quarters can outweigh Q4; publication month and reference quarter differ.')
amend('june',3,'Regarding the announced Census schedule: (1) 1 March 2027 is the general reference date. (2) 1 October 2026 applies to specified snow-bound areas. (3) All enumeration must occur on the reference date itself. Which are correct?','1 and 2 only','1 only|2 and 3 only|1, 2 and 3','Reference dates anchor particulars, not a claim that every household is counted on one day. Both geographic/reference-date qualifications matter.')
amend('june',4,'Consider the June SEZ changes: (1) The 10-hectare relaxation is sector-specific. (2) It removes every duty on transfers to the Domestic Tariff Area. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The semiconductor/component relaxation should not be generalised to all zones. Applicable domestic-entry duties are not erased by the relaxation.')
amend('june',7,'For collateral lending, consider: (1) LTV compares loan value with the value of pledged collateral. (2) A tiered LTV direction necessarily grants the same ceiling to every loan regardless of purpose and size. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','LTV is a ratio, while eligibility, category and size bands determine the applicable regulatory ceiling. Collateral does not eliminate repayment risk.')
amend('june',15,'Consider restoration: (1) A high plantation count alone proves biodiversity recovery. (2) Species suitability and survival are relevant to ecological outcomes. Which are correct?','2 only','1 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Planting totals do not establish natural ecosystem function. The Green India linkage stresses landscape, survival and ecological suitability.')
amend('june',18,'Regarding Talliki Vandanam, consider: (1) ₹15,000 is the stated gross annual per-child support for eligible beneficiaries. (2) The general ₹2,000 deduction proves every case must receive exactly ₹13,000 net. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The six-page mirrored G.O.Ms.27 contains separate RTE fee and scholarship-related adjustments; admissions and record verification also affect disbursal. Official-host authentication remains pending.')
amend('june',22,'Consider Emergency safeguards: (1) Armed rebellion replaced internal disturbance as an Article 352 ground. (2) The right to move a court for enforcement of Articles 20 and 21 may be suspended under Article 359. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The 44th Amendment strengthened safeguards. Articles 20 and 21 are excluded from the Article 359 suspension mechanism.')
amend('june',25,'Consider Axiom-4: (1) Indian participation supplied microgravity/operational experience. (2) It demonstrated a completed Indian indigenous crewed launch under Gaganyaan. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Participation in an international private flight does not by itself establish indigenous crewed-launch readiness. June launch and July return are separate milestones.')
amend('june',26,'A finer numerical weather-model grid: (1) increases spatial detail represented by the model; (2) guarantees accurate forecasts at every village. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Resolution is not identical to predictive accuracy. Validation, observations, initial conditions and uncertainty remain important for BharatFS.')
amend('july',7,'Regarding India–UK CETA: (1) Negotiations concluded before the July signature. (2) Signature automatically made every product duty-free that day. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','May conclusion, July signature and subsequent entry into force are distinct. Schedules, origin rules and domestic procedures shape usable access.')
amend('july',9,'Regarding ELI: (1) Payroll registration necessarily means durable net job creation. (2) Component targets may overlap and should not be blindly added. Which are correct?','2 only','1 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Genuine additionality, retention and wages require evaluation. Formalisation can be valuable without being identical to a wholly new durable job.')
amend('july',12,'Consider the Cooperative Policy: (1) It is distinct from state cooperative legislation. (2) Approval automatically amends every state cooperative Act. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','National policy and applicable society laws operate at different levels; member control, audit and elections still need institutional safeguards.')
amend('july',13,'Consider NCDC finance: (1) A grant to NCDC can support greater borrowing. (2) Expected borrowing is identical to money already disbursed as grants to societies. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Institutional support, mobilisation and onward loans are distinct. Leverage introduces credit risk and repayment conditions rather than free money.')
amend('july',14,'Regarding PM Dhan Dhaanya: (1) It targets 100 districts. (2) ₹24,000 crore is the annual outlay in the official explainer. (3) The six-year approval proves every target was achieved in July. Which are correct?','1 and 2 only','1 only|2 and 3 only|1, 2 and 3','The annual amount must not be mistaken for a six-year aggregate. Convergence and district targeting are design features, not proof of completed outcomes.')
amend('july',19,'The RDI corpus: (1) is distinct from actual disbursement; (2) consists only of unrestricted grants for every applicant. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','A corpus finances specified channels including concessional loans and equity routes. Technical appraisal, governance and additionality remain necessary.')
amend('july',22,'Consider aggregator regulation: (1) A model central guideline can require state-level implementation decisions. (2) A state option necessarily legalises every private-motorcycle taxi nationwide. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Guidance and operative state permission differ. Licensing, local rules and service conditions must be checked.')
amend('july',24,'Regarding environmental appraisal: (1) Terms of Reference define EIA study scope. (2) Their issuance alone constitutes final environmental clearance and interstate allocation of water. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Study terms, environmental clearance and water entitlements are different. The PBLP returned proposal requires stage-specific interpretation.')
amend('july',26,'NISAR combines which instrument pairing?','L-band SAR and S-band SAR.','C-band SAR and X-band SAR.|Ku-band SAR and Ka-band SAR.|L-band SAR and only a visible-light camera.','The mission combines L- and S-band synthetic-aperture radar. It supports day/night and many cloud-condition observations; data still need calibration and interpretation.')
amend('july',29,'For the Maratha Military Landscapes inscription: (1) The twelve components count as one serial World Heritage property. (2) Gingee is in Tamil Nadu. Which are correct?','Both 1 and 2',choices,'Eleven components are in Maharashtra and one is Gingee in Tamil Nadu. Serial components do not each add a separate property to the national total.')
amend('august',1,'Consider the August MPC: (1) Repo remained 5.5%. (2) SDF remained 5.25%. (3) MSF and Bank Rate were 5.25%. Which are correct?','1 and 2 only','1 only|2 and 3 only|1, 2 and 3','MSF and Bank Rate were 5.75% in the corroborating resolution account. PRS’s 5.25% MSF figure is not copied as correct.')
amend('august',2,'For the August GDP release: (1) Q1 FY2025–26 covers April–June. (2) The 7.8% estimate was real GDP year-on-year growth. (3) It establishes identical income growth for every household. Which are correct?','1 and 2 only','1 only|2 and 3 only|1, 2 and 3','Quarter, price basis and vintage matter. GDP aggregates output and is not a guarantee of uniform household income gains.')
amend('august',7,'Regarding FREE-AI: (1) It is a committee report. (2) Every recommendation became binding merely on release. (3) Accuracy alone establishes fairness in lending. Which are correct?','1 only','1 and 2 only|2 and 3 only|1, 2 and 3','A committee report differs from adopted regulation. Governance also concerns bias, explainability, security, accountability and remedies.')
amend('august',9,'Regarding the 130th Amendment proposal in the August snapshot: (1) It had been introduced and referred to a Joint Committee. (2) Custody is identical to conviction. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','It was a Bill, not an enacted 130th Amendment Act. Removal from ministerial office, membership disqualification and criminal conviction are separate.')
amend('august',13,'Regarding revised SVANidhi: (1) The first two tranches are ₹15,000 and ₹25,000. (2) All three tranches are unconditional grants payable together. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The third remains ₹50,000. These are sequential repayable working-capital loans subject to scheme conditions.')
amend('august',14,'Regarding E-DRIVE: (1) The overall programme was extended to March 2028. (2) Every two/three-wheeler incentive window was identically extended. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The overall date and category-specific windows differ. The extension particularly concerns buses, trucks and testing capacity.')
amend('august',18,'Consider port governance: (1) Non-major is a legal/administrative category. (2) Every non-major port must have lower cargo capacity than every major port. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','Legal classification is not a universal ranking by size or cargo throughput; state/Union governance roles matter.')
amend('august',23,'Regarding online gaming: (1) A stake for expected monetary enrichment matters under the defined money-gaming category. (2) Calling a game skill-based necessarily excludes it from that category. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The framework distinguishes money gaming from qualifying e-sports/social games irrespective of a simplistic skill/chance distinction; later rules and litigation need checking.')
amend('august',26,'Regarding Annadata’s announced ₹20,000 annual package: (1) ₹14,000 is the state share and ₹6,000 the PM-Kisan share. (2) A ₹7,000 first instalment proves the entire annual amount was paid at launch. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The described first combined instalment is ₹5,000 state plus ₹2,000 Centre. Annual package, instalment and verified actual credits differ.')
amend('august',27,'Consider Stree Shakti: (1) Girls, women and transgender persons with AP domicile are covered subject to rules. (2) Zero fare means APSRTC incurs no operating cost. Which are correct?','1 only','2 only|Both 1 and 2|Neither 1 nor 2','The five service categories and identity conditions qualify coverage. Zero-fare tickets support government reimbursement; operating costs do not disappear.')
print('Reviewed 30 MCQs for plausible statement-based discriminators')
